 * x^2 + ....\n     Return derivative of this polynomial in the same form.\n    >>> derivative([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    [1, 4, 12, 20]\n    >>> derivative([1, 2, 3])\n    [2, 6]\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(xs) <= 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # The derivative of (a_i * x^i) is (i * a_i * x^(i-1)).\n    # The new coefficient for x^j is (j+1) * xs[j+1].\n    # We iterate from the second coefficient (xs[1]) onwards.\n    # The original index of the coefficient being processed is `idx + 1` from the derivative formula perspective.\n    # The 'power' multiplier is `idx` when using enumerate(xs[1:], start=1).\n    # So, for xs[1], idx is 1, new coefficient is 1 * xs[1].\n    # For xs[2], idx is 2, new coefficient is 2 * xs[2].\n    return [idx * coeff for idx, coeff in enumerate(xs[1:], start=1)]", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/63": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "class InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(message)\nclass InputValidator:\n    def validate(self, n):\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"n must be an int\")\n        if n < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be >= 0\")\n        return None\nclass FibFibCalculator:\n    def compute(self, n: int) -> int:\n        if n == 0:\n            return 0\n        if n == 1:\n            return 0\n        if n == 2:\n            return 1\n        return self.compute_iterative(n)\n\n    def compute_iterative(self, n: int) -> int:\n        # Initialize with the first three fibfib numbers: fibfib(0), fibfib(1), fibfib(2).\n        a, b, c = 0, 0, 1\n        # Iterate from n=3 up to the desired n, updating the rolling state.\n        for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n            a, b, c = b, c, a + b + c\n        return c\ndef fibfib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The FibFib number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci se